# Where the browser sends API requests.
#
#   (empty)            Same origin: requests go to "/api/..." on the site's own
#                      address. In development Vite proxies /api to the backend
#                      (see vite.config.js); in production the backend serves
#                      the site and the API together. Works from other devices
#                      and through tunnels with no extra setup. Recommended.
#
#   http://host:8000   A separate backend. The backend must then list this
#                      site's address in its ALLOWED_ORIGINS setting (CORS).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=